12:["Nightlife","International food","Rooftop bars","Vintage shopping"]
11:{"slug":"itaewon","name":"Itaewon","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519608487953-e999c86e7455?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's most international neighbourhood. A melting pot of cultures with rooftop bars, global restaurants, vintage shops and some of the city's best nightlife. Itaewon has reinvented itself multiple times and remains one of Seoul's most dynamic areas.","nearestMetro":"Itaewon (Line 6)","vibe":"Cosmopolitan & eclectic","bestFor":"$12","priceRange":"₩₩ – ₩₩₩₩"}
14:["Bars","Live music","Street art","Shopping"]
13:{"slug":"hongdae","name":"Hongdae","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1514933651103-005eec06c04b?w=1200&q=80","intro":"The beating heart of Seoul's indie culture. Named after Hongik University, this neighbourhood is defined by street performers, graffiti art, independent boutiques and a nightlife scene that runs until dawn. Always young, always loud.","nearestMetro":"Hongik University (Line 2)","vibe":"Creative & youthful","bestFor":"$14","priceRange":"₩ – ₩₩₩"}
16:["Cafes","Shopping","Fine dining","K-beauty"]
15:{"slug":"gangnam","name":"Gangnam","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559305616-3f99cd43e353?w=1200&q=80","intro":"South of the river and famous worldwide thanks to a certain song. Gangnam is Seoul's business and luxury district — designer boutiques, upscale cafes, K-beauty clinics and some of the city's best restaurants hide behind glass facades.","nearestMetro":"Gangnam (Line 2)","vibe":"Upscale & polished","bestFor":"$16","priceRange":"₩₩₩ – ₩₩₩₩"}
18:["Street food","Shopping","K-beauty","Tourism"]
17:{"slug":"myeongdong","name":"Myeongdong","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1498654896293-37aacf113fd9?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's ultimate shopping district and street food paradise. Myeongdong's neon-lit streets are packed with K-beauty stores, department stores and some of the best street food vendors in the city. Touristy but worth it.","nearestMetro":"Myeongdong (Line 4)","vibe":"Buzzing & commercial","bestFor":"$18","priceRange":"₩ – ₩₩₩"}
1a:["Culture","Tea","Art galleries","Souvenirs"]
19:{"slug":"insadong","name":"Insadong","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517154421773-0529f29ea451?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's cultural heart. Traditional teahouses, antique shops, art galleries and hanok alleyways make Insadong the place to experience old Korea in the middle of a modern city. Don't miss the Ssamziegil complex.","nearestMetro":"Anguk (Line 3)","vibe":"Traditional & artsy","bestFor":"$1a","priceRange":"₩₩"}
1c:["Fashion","Fine dining","People watching","K-pop culture"]
1b:{"slug":"apgujeong","name":"Apgujeong","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559305616-3f99cd43e353?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's most fashionable neighbourhood. Apgujeong Rodeo is where K-pop stars shop, where new restaurants open first and where Seoul's trend-conscious crowd comes to see and be seen.","nearestMetro":"Apgujeong Rodeo (Bundang Line)","vibe":"Trendy & luxurious","bestFor":"$1c","priceRange":"₩₩₩ – ₩₩₩₩"}
